From d00f2acd3fb5396e0ca32d849bbf99743ccd6e39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:25:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] Add the seed acceptance test and correct the provider
 comparison

The estimator tolerates a source that misses flights evenly and one that
reports the wrong unit; it fails only when a source misses more of one
carrier's flights than of its rival's on the same route.  Nothing a provider
advertises measures that, so measure it here.

AFAC publishes flights per route next to passengers per route, which is the
free contrast the test needs.  Under even coverage the ratio of a candidate's
flight count to AFAC's would be one constant on every route; it is not, and
how it varies across routes with different carrier mixes identifies a
per-carrier coverage factor.  Alternating weighted least squares recovers it.
The tests inject a known bias, including the profile measured on OpenSky, and
check it comes back -- a detector that cannot do that would licence a purchase.

Correct the cost in the doc: AeroDataBox covers the whole national market for
USD 7.50 a month, not the USD 50-200 previously written, and its free tier is
the only one that includes historical data, so it is the one to trial.
AviationStack's free plan excludes historical flights, schedules and routes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
